From b23b3b80e04f3b3dfa18d015e7c4c6280fafa73f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:57:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 34/53] B70-PLE-RAM: native INT8 PLE table in pinned host RAM
 (B70_PLE_INT8=1, port of Lumnus 0008)

PLE is either RAM native or on SSD. B70_PLE_INT8=1 (+ B70_PLE_INT8_PATH)
selects Qwen4ExpPLEInt8RAMEmbedding: each TP rank reads its owned row range of
the INT8 row-scale table (160 int8 + fp32 scale = 164 B/row) once at boot into
pinned slabs and addresses rows directly by id (row - tp_start). No row cache,
no slot map, no reader on the step path. B70_PLE_INT8=1 together with
B70_PLE_INT8_NVME=1 raises at init.

- ple_ram.py (host-only, numpy): PleRamTable, plan_slabs. Slabs fill a power of
  two to within one row (max 8 GiB, tail < 1 MiB): the torch caching host
  allocator rounds each pinned request up to a power of two, so one 12.2 GiB
  slab per TP4 rank would pin 16 GiB. Load reuses ple_nvme.preload_range
  (O_DIRECT 64 MiB chunks, B70_PLE_INT8_LOAD_THREADS / _LOAD_CHUNK_MIB).
- b70_ple_ram.py: subclass of the 0.32 NVMe class; the host-prepared
  producer/consumer is inherited, _fill_stage gathers from RAM. Boot checks:
  every owned scale finite and >= 0 (0008's full scan), B70_PLE_INT8_BOOT_SAMPLE
  rows vs O_DIRECT row reads, BF16 cross-check with PLE_TABLE_PATH. One line per
  rank: "B70 PLE INT8 RAM (rank r): N rows, X GiB pinned, loaded in Y s ...".
- Gather: host gather into the pinned stage + one H2D, then the existing eager
  consumer (int8 byte-sum all-reduce, per-row q*s dequant to BF16). The ids are
  already on the host (B70_PLE_HOST_IDS=1), so no extra sync; 0008's UVA Triton
  gather is not used (one PCIe read per 164-B row, and the 0.32 pinned-UVA class
  has not run on XPU).
- b70_ple_nvme.py: flag/label made class attributes, the BF16 cross-check
  factored into bf16_crosscheck (NVMe behaviour unchanged).

Tests: tests/b70/test_ple_int8_ram.py, 25 passed + 1 skipped (real-table test,
needs B70_PLE_INT8_TEST_PATH). Existing PLE NVMe tests unchanged: 33 passed,
3 skipped.
